        "ephanna": "evidence_gap"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: In the Session 12 council chamber fight, it\u2019s the **Players**, **The Wolf**, **Thalia**, and **corrupted guards** (as active enemies/reinforcements).\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Participants (CANON + OBSERVED):\n  - **Players (group)** \u2014 present and actively confronting the situation; they recount their story to the council and are engaged when combat breaks out.\n  - **The Wolf** \u2014 explicitly in the **Council Room** and the central adversary of the encounter.\n  - **Thalia (Commander of the Guard)** \u2014 present with the Wolf (\u201cWolf is standing at Thalia\u2019s shoulder\u201d) and can be influenced or act in combat (including attacking under his direction).\n  - **Corrupted guards** \u2014 part of the encounter by design (\u201cplayers confront The Wolf and corrupted guards in the council chamber\u201d), with additional reinforcements implied as the fight escalates.\n\n- Notably Absent / Unconfirmed:\n  - No explicit confirmation that **other council members** or **uncorrupted guards** remain present during the fight (they may have been there earlier, but not stated as active participants in the combat snapshot).\n\n- Encounter Framing (CANON):\n  - The fight is defined as a confrontation with **The Wolf and corrupted guards**, with escalating tension as more enemies arrive.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
