      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Headmaster Tinkerbright speaks for the wizards; he views the cult\u2019s magic as a dangerous perversion and pushes for aggressive arcane detection and containment measures.\n\nHeadmaster Tinkerbright (CANON/OBSERVED) is the Wizard\u2019s College representative on the council. As Headmaster and a brilliant arcane authority, he is positioned as the primary voice of the wizard faction.\n\nHis angle on the cult is strongly interventionist:\n- He sees the corrupted meat and the cult\u2019s work as a \u201cperversion of magic\u201d (CANON).\n- He takes the threat to the city very seriously and is deeply troubled by the dark magic involved (CANON).\n- He advocates deploying Wizard\u2019s College resources to detect and counteract the cult (OBSERVED).\n- His concrete plans include a magical lockdown and using runes or detection spells to locate corruption (OBSERVED/CANON).\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Head of the Wizard\u2019s College; arcane representative on the council  \n- Alignment/Outlook: Anti-cult, views their magic as dangerous corruption  \n- Strategy: Magical detection, city lockdown, proactive arcane intervention  \n- Personality Notes: Brilliant, inventive, but can be distracted by experiments",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
