      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf ends the council-chamber fight dead\u2014**\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d**\u2014with Bonogo taking the head; earlier escape/invisibility reflects mid-fight actions, not the final state.\n\nThe projection shows conflicting OBSERVED states: the Wolf both **\u201cescapes\u201d / \u201cInvisible\u201d** and is **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d** The later, terminal outcome takes precedence, reinforced by **ent_bonogo**: \u201cRemoved the Wolf\u2019s head to transport it.\u201d That indicates the fight ultimately concludes with the Wolf killed and physically secured (at least his head) by Bonogo.\n\nSo while the Wolf *did* attempt to flee using invisibility and a secret passage during the encounter, that escape did not stick\u2014he is no longer at large by the end of the scene.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Outcome: **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d** (OBSERVED, terminal)\n- Body status: Head taken by Bonogo (OBSERVED)\n- Prior state during fight: Invisible, attempting escape via secret passage (OBSERVED)\n- Role: Central adversary in the council chamber battle (CANON)",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
