      "answer": "TL;DR: Thalia is **not corrupted like the guards**\u2014she is **ensorcelled by the Wolf**, which is a different effect.\n\nThalia\u2019s condition is explicitly distinct from the guards:\n- Guards show corruption via **\u201can oily sheen to their eyes\u201d** and physical mutation/merging with cult influence (OBSERVED).\n- Thalia **\u201cdoes not have an oily sheen to her eyes\u201d** and is instead **\u201censorcelled by the Wolf\u201d** (OBSERVED).\n\nThis is reinforced by her behavior and mental state:\n- Her **charmed status ended** and she can **realize how dire the situation truly is**, suggesting external influence rather than internal corruption.\n- She can be **convinced of the Wolf\u2019s betrayal**, which wouldn\u2019t align with full corruption.\n\nSo in the fight, her attacking the party comes from **magical influence/control (ensorcellment)** tied to the Wolf, not the same corruption affecting the guards.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Physical Condition: No oily sheen; **ensorcelled by the Wolf** (OBSERVED)\n- Mental State: Influenced but capable of clarity; charm can end (OBSERVED)\n- Relationship to Wolf: Serves him under influence; directly manipulated (OBSERVED)\n- Guards Contrast: Corrupted with oily sheen and physical changes (OBSERVED)",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
