      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The council room fights back with arcane traps (force bursts + paralysis), falling debris, and disorienting magical effects tied to illusions and the room\u2019s humming mechanisms\u2014especially punishing anyone without amulets.\n\nThe room itself is actively hostile in a few concrete ways:\n\n- **Arcane trap bursts (CANON/OBSERVED)**: The space can trigger bursts that **deal 2d6 force damage and can temporarily paralyze** the players. Per CANON, these traps may specifically target anyone **without the amulets**.\n\n- **Falling debris hazards (OBSERVED)**: The environment can physically break apart mid-fight, **forcing players to dodge falling debris**, disrupting positioning and actions.\n\n- **Illusions / spatial disorientation (CANON)**: Players are already **disoriented by illusory walls/illusion spells**, meaning movement, line of sight, and targeting can be unreliable.\n\n- **Ambient mechanical/magical feedback (CANON)**: The **constant hum of wall-embedded gears** shifts; players might notice **an unusual change in the hum when something significant happens**, signaling traps, triggers, or phase changes.\n\n- **Auditory pressure (CANON)**: **Footsteps echoing** can imply incoming reinforcements, adding stress and urgency even mid-fight.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Arcane traps (force + paralysis), amulet-sensitive targeting  \n- Hazards: Falling debris  \n- Magical Effects: Illusory walls causing disorientation  \n- Environmental Signals: Shifting hum, echoing footsteps indicating changes or threats",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
