      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Delay lets the cult advance their plan\u2014using hidden routes and possible council influence\u2014to sabotage the city and push toward summoning the flesh kaiju while the city edges closer to disaster.\n\nIf the council keeps stalling, the biggest risk is momentum shifting fully to **the cult**.  \n- CANON: The cult is actively **using hidden routes** beneath the city and can **switch to alternative routes if blocked**, so inaction doesn\u2019t slow them\u2014it gives them freedom to maneuver.  \n- CANON: Their goals include **accessing the heart of the city**, **corrupting cauldrons**, and **summoning the flesh kaiju**.  \n- CANON/OBSERVED: They also have **influence in the council**, meaning delay may actively benefit them politically, not just tactically.\n\nAt the city level:  \n- OBSERVED: The city is already **\u201cbrought closer to disaster by each failed or unresolved debate.\u201d**  \n- CANON: Weak points in defenses and reliance on coordinated response (like a **planned magical lockdown**) mean hesitation creates exploitable gaps.\n\nFor the players:  \n- OBSERVED: They are **delayed by lengthy deliberation**, which directly costs them the chance to intercept cult operations in motion.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Cult Goals: Summoning, sabotage, infiltration  \n- City Defenses: Vulnerable, considering lockdown  \n- City Operational Status: Escalating toward disaster with inaction  \n- Cult Positioning: Underground, mobile via hidden infrastructure  \n- Political Risk: Cult influence inside the council",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
