      "answer": "TL;DR: The Council Room shows signs of a chaotic, deceptive fight\u2014most notably that the Wolf is **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d**, with lingering confusion from his illusions and evidence he attempted escape via a hidden route.\n\nBased on OBSERVED facts, the clearest, current state is that the Wolf has been killed and physically altered: **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d** Additionally, Bonogo explicitly **removed the Wolf\u2019s head to transport it**, so the body and head are no longer together (and may not both be present).\n\nYou should emphasize:\n- Signs of a frantic struggle tied to the Wolf\u2019s tactics: he **creates illusory duplicates**, so the room likely feels disorienting in hindsight\u2014overturned positions, conflicting lines of attack, or uncertainty about where he \u201creally\u201d was.\n- Evidence of an escape attempt: the Wolf was **attempting to escape through a secret passage while invisible**, so clues like a disturbed exit, opened/ajar hidden access, or scuffed flooring near the council chamber are appropriate.\n- The aftermath of urgency: he was **desperate, begging to be killed**, which can color the emotional tone of the space.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Physical Condition: \u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d\n- Tactics/Effects: Illusory duplicates caused confusion\n- Movement: Attempted escape via secret passage while invisible\n- Tone: Chaotic, deceptive, urgent confrontation aftermath",
      "embedding_similarity": null
