      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf is dead \u2014 specifically **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d** \u2014 and had signs of corruption prior to death (oily sheen in eyes).\n\nThe most current **OBSERVED** state at end of Session 12 shows a clear terminal outcome: **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d** This overrides earlier states like escaping, invisibility, or active manipulation, since those occurred before the killing blow.\n\nCorruption-wise, the Wolf **did have \u201can oily sheen to his eyes\u201d** (OBSERVED), which is consistent with other corrupted individuals. There is no explicit note that this corruption was removed upon death, so his body likely remains corrupted, just no longer active.\n\nHis mental state before death (begging to be killed, regretful, desperate) reinforces that he was still under some influence or aware of it when he died.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Physical Condition: **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d**, previously showed \u201coily sheen to his eyes\u201d\n- Alignment/Role: Cultist, saboteur, betrayer of Mirathorn\n- Mental State (pre-death): Desperate, regretful, begging for death\n- Narrative Status: Dead; viable target for Speak with Dead (per player plans)",
