      "answer": "TL;DR: Before the council fight, the Wolf is an active, deceptive infiltrator manipulating events; after, he is **decapitated; head removed from body**, shifting from a manipulative threat to a defeated (but revealing) figure.\n\nBefore the council fight (OBSERVED + CANON):\n- The Wolf is a **saboteur and cultist**, actively working to mislead the council and players.\n- Uses **illusory duplicates** and deception to create confusion and avoid detection.\n- Holds authority as **second-in-command of the guard**, enabling influence over city governance.\n- Actively **manipulates Commander Thalia Ashenvale** (ensorcelled) and attempts to steer decisions.\n- Operationally mobile: uses **Invisibility**, attempts escape via secret tunnels, and directs others (e.g., orders Thalia to attack).\n\nAfter the council fight (OBSERVED):\n- His physical state is **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d** (terminal outcome).\n- No longer an active combatant or manipulator.\n- His prior desperation and regret (begging to be killed/released) become more relevant post-mortem, especially with player plans to use **Speak with Dead**.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Enemy \u2192 defeated adversary\n- Operational Status: Escaping, deceptive \u2192 neutralized\n- Physical Condition: Invisible, mobile \u2192 **decapitated; head removed from body**\n- Influence: Active manipulation \u2192 only informational (via corpse)\n- Tactics: Illusions, deception \u2192 none (post-death)",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
