      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Thalia was **not corrupted**\u2014she was **ensorcelled (magically manipulated) by the Wolf**, meaning she was being played rather than willingly complicit.\n\nThalia\u2019s state is consistently described as **\u201censorcelled by the Wolf\u201d (OBSERVED + CANON)** and **\u201cinnocent\u201d (OBSERVED)**. Crucially, **\u201cThalia does not have an oily sheen to her eyes\u201d (OBSERVED)**, which distinguishes her from genuinely corrupted individuals like affected guards. This indicates she was not physically or spiritually corrupted in the same way.\n\nHer behavior\u2014defending the guard, downplaying the threat, and even **attacking the group after the Wolf's instruction (OBSERVED)**\u2014comes from that magical influence. CANON further clarifies she was **\u201censorcelled\u2026 to overlook corruption within the guard\u201d**, and OBSERVED notes she **\u201chas no idea they are being manipulated by the Wolf.\u201d**\n\nThere is also progression: **\u201cCharmed status ended\u201d and \u201crealizes how dire the situation truly is\u201d (OBSERVED)**. This confirms the influence can break, reinforcing that it was external control, not internal corruption.\n\nThe Wolf\u2019s role: he is a **cultist saboteur using deception and control**, directly **issuing orders to Thalia** and exploiting her position as Commander of the Guard.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Thalia condition: Ensorcelled, not corrupted; no oily sheen\n- Agency: Compromised by the Wolf\u2019s magic\n- Alignment: Innocent, duty-driven\n- Wolf connection: Direct magical manipulation and command influence\n- Resolution state: Charm can/end did end, restoring awareness",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    }
